A||||6||zebrex||performance gain by making air passage larger||||5||
Z||000000||zebrex||03-15-2000||11:31 PM||||I heard the hiss of air being sucked into the vent right behind the drivers door so I pulled the cover off. The opening is about the size of a pencil. Would I notice a hp gain If I made this opening larger? also is there an easy or wrong way to do this (aka dremel tool) I quess what im asking is. Can just that blocking blate be removed or should it be?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Linx||03-16-2000||12:03 AM||||nah- dont bother enlarging it.  it aint hissin' from the air passin' thru that body panel inlet.  It's hissin' as it passes thru the manifold throttle body plate.  You're just <I>hearin'</I> the noise thru the body panel intake.<P>take off the filter-to-manifold hose  and you'll hear it in all it's glory.  it's loud.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mwbackus||03-16-2000||03:01 AM||||I believe the plate you are referring to is the water separator.  Many choose to remove this as it does seem likely that it interferes with the flow of intake air.  Probably wont see much difference, but ever little bit helps.  Using the end of a hammer to bust the plate out is the most popular method.  Just dont drive in hurricanes..<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000003||WKDFIRO||03-16-2000||10:55 AM||||I have had a straight tube (got it from Home Depot for $2.50 its some kind of wide diameter irrigationg tube...)on my 87 4 cyl and now on my 85 GT and have never had a problem with water. The path it must travel to actually get in to the engine is a tough gravity defying one even at high speed, (I still have the stock air filter canister etc.) I would recommend taking off the wheel well and putting in a tube. The sound you get alone is worth the price of admission!||||reg||14
Z||000004||DaRkLoRD||03-16-2000||06:48 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by WKDFIRO:<BR><B>The sound you get alone is worth the price of admission!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Is it sort of a cool hissing sound? (how loud?) if so, that's a mod I'd like to do..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I'd probably replace the stock airbox with a big K&N filter however.<P><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 03-16-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||WKDFIRO||03-16-2000||06:55 PM||||The guy I work for did that for his 86 SE w/ 3.4. He fabricated a tube going straight into the intake area with a K&N. It hisses very loudly! A little too much for me.  Its hard to say how much better the K&N would be from the straight tube, (I would imagine quite a bit more though)because he also put on 4.10 gears at the same time so its hard to tell how much the intake gave and how much the gearing gives.<P>I prefer mine because I kinda like that Ram Air thing. I love putting my hand on the intake and rev it and feel the suction from the intake. Huge improvement from what can be described as an intake muffler either way.<p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 03-16-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000006||Bruce||03-16-2000||09:32 PM||||WKDFiero,<BR>Can you elaborate on the tube you installed, e.g.: diameter, length, etc.?<BR>Thanks.||||reg||1
